  "id": 3,
  "name": "return_regret_hybrid",
  "intent": "This hybrid heuristic balances immediate distance, return-to-start proximity, and regret. The return term (0.2 * return_distance) encourages exploration away from the start, while the regret term (0.3 * regret) rewards candidates with a significantly closer nearest unvisited neighbor, promoting selection of well-connected hubs. This combination aims to improve performance on uniform instances where the parent is weaker, by reducing future travel costs.",
